  "worked_solution": "First, we cancel any terms that appear in both a numerator of one fraction and a denominator of the other one. Then, we multiply the numerators and the denominators as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11p{q}^{2}}{{r}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{5{r}^{2}}{121{p}^{4}q} & =\\frac{11pq\\cdot q}{r\\cdot {r}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{5\\cdot {r}^{2}}{11pq\\cdot 11{p}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{11pq}\\cdot q}{r\\cdot \\cancel{{r}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{5\\cdot \\cancel{{r}^{2}}}{\\cancel{11pq}\\cdot 11{p}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{q}{r}\\cdot \\frac{5}{11{p}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5q}{11{p}^{3}r}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
